      "claim": "The lord‑peasant relationship in medieval England was defined by feudal obligations rather than voluntary market contracts.",
      "evidence": "Manorial court rolls and customary law recorded fixed rents, labor services (corvée), and dues owed by serfs to their lord in exchange for protection and use of land.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": []
